<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 96,466 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 96,466 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 96,466 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday compared to 54,775 tonnes on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Thursday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			30,126	    25,945</p>
<p>    Import cargo			66,340	    28,830</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight ships were expected to sail and six to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		 16,500	 Bunga Cenderewasih 28/2</p>
<p>Chemicals		 9,900	 NCC Najd		1/3</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     27,000	 Philadelphia	  4/3</p>
<p>Containers		  400	 Energy		 28/2</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
